cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GLASS in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GLASS: A Transparent Perpetual-Futures Market Simulator for Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning"
abstract: >-
  GLASS is an open, reproducible agent-based simulator of a perpetual-futures
  exchange with margin, liquidation cascades, auto-deleveraging, funding and an
  index price, in which market transparency (anonymous, attributed, or fully
  public positions) is an experimental variable. It provides a heterogeneous
  scripted trader ecology, a Gymnasium environment, a multi-agent PPO trainer
  and an evaluation protocol with paired held-out seeds.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mantovani
    given-names: Martino
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dudenfa/glass-sim"
keywords:
  - market simulation
  - limit order book
  - perpetual futures
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - market transparency
